---
source: tests/release_workflow.rs
expression: rendered
---
echo "::notice title=Release automation is not configured::release-please did not run; see the job log for the two credentials a maintainer has to add."
cat <<'NOTICE'
This repository has no release credentials, so the release-please job was
skipped rather than failed. Nothing is broken and nothing is pending.

To turn release automation on, a maintainer with admin rights does three things:

  1. Install the release-please GitHub App on P4suta/ginary, granting it
     contents: write, pull-requests: write and issues: write.
  2. Add the repository variable RELEASE_PLEASE_APP_CLIENT_ID, set to the
     App's client id.
  3. Add the repository secret RELEASE_PLEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY, set to the
     App's private key.

The default GITHUB_TOKEN is deliberately not an alternative: this repository
sets can_approve_pull_request_reviews to false, so GitHub Actions may not
create pull requests, and that hardening stays.
NOTICE
